      "side": 1,
      "message": "When chipset enters S5 state (pd_chipset_shutdown()) DRP state is set to PD_DRP_FORCE_SINK and PD_EVENT_UPDATE_DUAL_ROLE is set.\n\ntc_event_check() function sees that PD_EVENT_UPDATE_DUAL_ROLE is set and calls pd_update_dual_role_config() which changes state to Unattached.SNK because current power role is PD_ROLE_SOURCE, and PD_DRP_FORCE_SINK is set.\n\nIn Unattached.SNK state it goes to LowPowerMode state (because PD_DRP_FORCE_SINK), which is immediately followed by DRPAutoToogle state.\n\nIn DRPAutoToggle state drp_auto_toggle_next_state() returns DRP_TC_UNATTACHED_SNK, but tc_drp_auto_toggle_run() jumps to TC_ATTACH_WAIT_SNK.\n\nIn AttachWait.SNK we jump to Unattached.SRC because both pins are not RP. Comment in this function says that we should transition to Unattached.SNK, maybe this is the bug I was looking for. Furthermore DRP state is still PD_DRP_FORCE_SINK.\n\nFrom Unattached.SRC it jumps to AttachWait.SRC, because one of CC pins are RD, then it goes directly to Attached.SRC \n\n\nVoila!",
      "parentUuid": "306d013c_b479d755",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 16,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 17,
        "endChar": 40
      },
      "revId": "d8dcf3b7d41d4579913396fe06d4f253fe7b33f8",
